# The one Chromium build scorsese renders `html` clips with (#594, #772).
#
# `chrome-headless-shell` from Chrome for Testing, at one version for every
# platform and every way scorsese runs: CI's goldens (#775), the desktop and
# CLI first-use download (#776) and the web image (#778) all read this file,
# never a copy of it. A golden pins Chromium version + raster mode (#606), so
# two version numbers in two places would be two sets of pixels.
#
# 154.0.8037.92 is the build #606 measured every determinism, memory and speed
# figure on, and #772 measured CI against (its results comment). Moving it
# means re-measuring that, and re-blessing every `html` golden.
#
# The format is the narrowest both readers share: `KEY=value` lines, no quotes,
# no spaces, `#` comments. A shell sources it (`. tools/chromium/pin`); Rust
# reads it with `include_str!` and splits each line on its first `=`. In the
# URL, `{version}` and `{platform}` are placeholders for the reader to fill.
# Each checksum is the sha256 of that platform's zip, exactly as downloaded.

CHROME_VERSION=154.0.8037.92
CHROME_URL=https://storage.googleapis.com/chrome-for-testing-public/{version}/{platform}/chrome-headless-shell-{platform}.zip
